            "additionalParams": true,
            "hint": {
              "label": "Usage Guide",
              "value": "\n## 🎮 Discord Bot Setup & Token Guide\n\n### Step 1: Create Discord Bot & Get Token\n1. Go to [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications).\n2. Click **New Application** ➔ enter a name ➔ go to **Bot** tab on the left menu.\n3. Click **Reset Token** (or Copy Token) and paste it into the **Bot Token** field below.\n4. **ENABLE INTENT**: Under **Privileged Gateway Intents**, turn **ON** `MESSAGE CONTENT INTENT` and click **Save Changes**.\n\n### Step 2: Get Channel ID & Invite Bot\n1. In Discord app Settings ➔ **Advanced** ➔ turn **ON** `Developer Mode`.\n2. Right-click your target Discord channel ➔ click **Copy Channel ID** ➔ paste into **Channel ID** field below.\n3. In Discord Developer Portal ➔ **OAuth2** ➔ **URL Generator**:\n   - Check `bot` under Scopes.\n   - Check `Send Messages` and `Read Message History` under Bot Permissions.\n   - Copy the generated URL and paste it in your browser to invite the bot to your Discord server!\n\n### Step 3: Activate & Test Live\n1. Toggle the workflow to **ACTIVE** in the canvas header!\n2. MicroMind connects via live WebSocket Gateway and auto-replies to any message typed in the channel!\n"
